# HTTP port the service listens on.
PORT=3000

# Log level: fatal | error | warn | info | debug | trace
LOG_LEVEL=info

# Postgres — the default datastore. This value matches docker-compose's dev
# instance (`bun db:start`). The live-test instance is a DIFFERENT database
# on 5433 (ar_live) and is set by `bun run test:live` — never point
# this at it.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://ar:ar@localhost:5432/ar

# Redis — OFF by default. Uncomment to register the Redis dependency
# (start the instance with `docker compose --profile redis up -d`).
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

# Bearer-token auth by RFC 7662 introspection — OFF by default; both values
# are required to enable it, and it is read only when the local credential
# strategy below is NOT configured. That pair takes precedence, and the
# framework schema refuses a service carrying both forms at once.
#
# The URL is a SIBLING deployment's introspection endpoint, never this
# service's own: `/auth` is mounted only when the basic pair is set, which
# is exactly when this pair goes unread. See src/auth/ and the README
# ("What's wired" — Auth).
#
# `AUTH_INTROSPECT_SECRET` has a second job independent of the URL — it is
# also the secret this service demands on its OWN POST /auth/introspect, so
# a deployment running the basic strategy sets it alone to let a sibling
# ask about the tokens minted here.
# AUTH_INTROSPECT_URL=https://sibling-service.internal/auth/introspect
# AUTH_INTROSPECT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-32+-character-random-secret

# Local credential strategy (basic auth) — OFF by default; both values
# are required to enable it. Set both and the service upserts one operator
# row into `auth_users` on every boot, mounts POST /auth/login, /auth/logout
# and /auth/introspect, and verifies its own tokens in-process, taking
# precedence over the introspection pair above. Run `bun run db:migrate`
# first: the bootstrap needs the auth tables to already exist.
#
# Left valueless deliberately: this file is TRACKED and is copied
# verbatim by whoever stands the stack up, so a password written here
# follows the README onto every machine set up the same way. The real
# values belong in `.env` (gitignored) or in the launching environment.
#
# Floors, enforced at boot: `AUTH_BASIC_USER` at least 1 character,
# `AUTH_BASIC_PASSWORD` at least 12. Uncommenting either and leaving it
# blank fails the boot rather than reading as nothing set.
# AUTH_BASIC_USER=
# AUTH_BASIC_PASSWORD=

# How long a minted session token stays valid, in seconds — 86400 (24
# hours) when unset. Written into the session row at mint time, so a change
# reaches only sessions issued afterwards and live ones keep the expiry they
# were given. Valueless for the same reason as the pair above, this file
# being copied verbatim; an uncommented blank is a boot failure, not a fall
# back to the default.
# AUTH_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS=

# n8n instance the operator commands talk to — OFF by default. `AR_N8N_URL`
# is the base URL of that instance's public REST API; `AR_N8N_API_KEY` is
# the key it issued for those commands to authenticate with. The running
# service opens neither, so leaving both unset changes nothing a boot does.
# Both are left valueless rather than carrying an example of their own:
# this file is TRACKED and is copied verbatim by whoever stands the stack
# up, so a URL or a key written here follows the README onto every machine
# set up the same way. The values belong in `.env` (gitignored) or in the
# launching environment, never in a tracked file.
# AR_N8N_URL=
# AR_N8N_API_KEY=

# MCP entrypoint (src/mcp/index.ts): 'stdio' for Claude Desktop / MCP
# Inspector; unset for HTTP.
# MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio
